==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Souma & Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Cat-Eared Souma''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Souma's range of 440 is appealing, especially against many melee Alien and Angel enemies. With this, he can stand safely to slow and weaken many otherwise threatening enemies. However, as each status condition only has a 50% chance of occurring, he cannot always be relied on, and should instead be used as backup for more consistent de-buffers such as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo]], [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer]].

His damage also allows him to function as a decently strong backline attacker, in a similar way as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]].

==='''True Form'''===
Cat-Eared Souma now targets Floating enemies, where his range of 440 grants him many more targets. These include most variants of [[Teacher Bun Bun]] and even the [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s. In fact, the only Cyclones that he can't really control are [[The Perfect Cyclone]] because of range and those Cyclones outside of his target traits ([[Zyclone]], [[Primeval Cyclone]], [[Aku Cyclone]]).

Additionally, his crowd control abilities are guaranteed, thus making him far more reliable at stalling. In fact, with Slow-boosting [[Cat Combo]]s and [[Treasure]]s, he can even perma-slow enemies that he can outrange, thus improving his usage tremendously and letting him serve as the main support unit instead of backup for other crowd controllers.

==='''Talents'''===
'''[[Curse]]''' is an interesting talent, as Angels and especially Aliens are notorious for abusing various abilities that it can disable. However, despite also occurring at 100% chance, it isn't as viable on Souma due to its very short uptime (even with a massive NP investment), made worse by his long time between attacks (nearly 9 seconds), allowing enemies a large window of opportunity to potentially recuperate.

'''Curse Immunity''' has very few viable applications. While it seems useful for a CC unit like Souma, he does not target Relics, so this restricts him to stages with the [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]] that mix threats within his target traits, even though it's easier to fight outside of its effective range. No Angels and Aliens employ Curse, and while Othom is a Floating enemy that Souma cannot outrange, he is too fragile to be useful against Othom. Even then, Othom's Curse does not have full uptime in itself, making this talent redundant.

'''Dodge''' does very little to improve Souma's survivability, as it has a very low activation chance of 20% and short duration of 2 seconds, ultimately contributing little compared to his CC.

'''Attack Buff''' and '''Defense Buff''' do help with Souma's utility, but are again held back by the fact he lacks any damage/health-boosting abilities.

